        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 8,
        "titulo": "Frequency and the double negative",
        "explicacao": "The adverbs of frequency form a scale: всегда (always), часто (often), иногда (sometimes), редко (rarely), никогда (never). In Russian, when «никогда» is there, the verb takes «не» as well: «Я никогда не читаю», literally «I never don't read». In English we say just «I never read». This is called the double negative, and in Russian it is compulsory.",
        "comparacao": "Non-standard English also stacks negatives («I don't never read»), but in Russian this is the standard rule: «не» is always required.",
